         <div class="guide-eyebrow">New York State · Parent Guides</div>
         <h1>The CSE Meeting: A Complete Guide for NY Parents</h1>
         <p class="guide-intro">
            Your child's CSE meeting is one of the most consequential meetings you'll ever sit in. This guide explains what it is, who must be in the room, how to prepare, what your rights are, and the red flags that tell you something is wrong — all in plain language.
         </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Table of Contents -->
      <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
         <div class="toc-title">On This Page</div>
         <ol>
            <li><a href="#what-is-cse">What is a CSE meeting?</a></li>
            <li><a href="#who-attends">Who must attend</a></li>
            <li><a href="#prepare">How to prepare</a></li>
            <li><a href="#your-rights">Your rights in the room</a></li>
            <li><a href="#iep-sections">Reading the IEP document</a></li>
